e91uMmqN3ovwfNWKoFuOqPgDyW9QkgXCVI8rGYSfD_SzJJ-kQUmcMLpHBAWUfS0QpFaBotcG3q1kxKLZh48ea6vzxz4dzXZQtfvWNb3reFPFVtpVFMpgiYMwIyIUSfIFxqlKY\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Tito Ramos\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV2kv3D0Xh-TOAMpA8AsrtivnGT5jniD_h3TEih0dWEPWCzURW8Lg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:1020:\"The Clean Fuel station at the TPLEX Rotunda in Rosario, La Union is a convenient and well-maintained pit stop for travelers. The place is spacious, organized, and true to the Clean Fuel standard — everything looks neat and well-kept. The staff are polite, prompt, and professional, making refueling quick and hassle-free.\n\nWhat stands out is the ample parking space and the variety of local eateries and food stalls surrounding the area. It’s a great spot to take a break, stretch your legs, and grab a quick meal before getting back on the road — definitely a plus for long drives.\n\nThe only downside is that restroom access is limited to Clean Fuel card members, which can be a bit inconvenient for non-members. For a major highway stop, it would be more traveler-friendly if basic facilities were open to everyone.\n\nOverall: A clean, spacious, and reliable station with excellent service and convenient nearby dining options. If not for the restroom restriction, it would easily be a top-rated stop along TPLEX.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2025-10-29T11:44:27.433038660Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"Marc Jimenez\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV6hmLGEhPgJ_LScXBzsk1vagUWhEP0MqelZ40M5NpfeVDJCMHg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:224:\"The washroom is clean, but you need a receipt to access it. There\'s Shakeys, Tapa King, and other food options (we went here at 6:30am, but they are closed).  The only open establishment here at that time is the korean mart.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"