gjnNQb6vuTlodV1hFbPNevF5k1QC3MyrvrQXa5b6KQNsVh3YQBNI4xapcNpXELPvkqMOFmxqISmnkdJlAGkUBp-1jb7rEM_BolQE14ZHMG9WHoRL2fo73GOHzfpUEqUMwUaw_q04yr8DoETJMbutmtXh8vL9eycmU6Qg96db7BfsqQxz4IFh5x2lX2ITJmQz9vDui-PrYDdxwg2kvmHSPlgxsGM-3Yp5ytsnYoGsKlq1kETE3m1QK0MsXHXYJM6UN5A\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:26:\"Kshitija Suryawanshi Patil\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV636asBCAmt-ms3wzBOhVknsc36nirCAqHK13N7ALL2_QZuGRh=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:1745:\"Fort Santiago stands as an undeniably captivating historical gem nestled within the venerable walls of Intramuros, and without a doubt, it proved to be a resounding highlight of my entire visit to Manila. While a swift exploration could certainly be accomplished in under an hour, I made a deliberate choice to immerse myself fully in its rich tapestry of history. Consequently, I spent well over an hour, allowing myself the luxury of unhurriedly traversing the expansive grounds, delving into every intriguing corner, and truly appreciating the profound historical context that permeates every stone and pathway.\nThe entire area of Fort Santiago is remarkably well-maintained, a testament to its preservation. Its layout facilitates an effortless and engaging exploration, with numerous thoughtfully placed spots inviting visitors to pause, reflect, and absorb the atmosphere. At each of these vantage points, detailed historical markers provide invaluable insights, enriching the experience with narratives of past events and significant figures. Furthermore, these locations often offer breathtaking views along the tranquil River Pasig, a serene contrast to the fort’s dramatic past. This combination of educational enlightenment and peaceful contemplation creates a unique ambiance. It serves as both an enlightening journey through history and a surprisingly tranquil oasis, offering a stark and welcome contrast to the often frenetic energy of the bustling city that lies just beyond the ancient walls. The quietude within its ramparts allows for a moment of reflection, a chance to step back in time and connect with the stories etched into this significant landmark, making it an essential and memorable part of any Manila itinerary.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-30T05:47:41.602652759Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:7:\"romaisa\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV3s6uALfNeGe4va56As1Bs6AtJJitB6yY7wxMyInUOk0t-VOM=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:355:\"Lines can be long on weekends. There’s a park near the entrance of Fort Santiago where you can watch folk dance shows and have a picnic.\n\nYou will learn a lot about the Spanish colonial period in this place. After finishing the museum tour, there’s also an area at the top where you can hang around and enjoy the view of the Pasig River. A must visit!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-29T03:46:13.464359894Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:8:\"joe mazi\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIcoM1iOyyAlAz7vsGnRZk4Y9LwNyxWn6GfyHXghTpYGWkrJw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:239:\"Very much of a historical area. I was amazed to this type of Spanish fort in the Philippines. I spent the whole day walking around the historic place. I did take a personal tour guided morning. It cost 3500 pesos. It was worth every penny.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-04T02:48:43.004297629Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:17:\"Conrad Harrington\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKEgTYVWkx5Sv3yGX7ZaJnKSKXwteYfl1eySJQXh66M27wOGw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:3;s:4:\"text\";s:372:\"Worth a visit if you’re passing by or visiting multiple sites like Rizal park and the Basilica but not a destination on its own. All three sites are all in approximately 20 minutes walking distance from each other so you don’t need a tour guide.\nA pleasant place, very peaceful and a few nice affordable cafe’s and shops on site but probably around a 30 minute stay.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-14T11:46:17.083510518Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"Dr. Ajeet Singh\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUpvZJd9QbCCs3RIPR07wHOV8l34Wrku5kFcV4FnHvSLw5wsljkKA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:1225:\"We visited Fort Santiago in April 2026 and paid PHP 75 per person for admission.Fort Santiago is a powerful, well-preserved historical site inside Intramuros. Highlights:Ticket and parking: Admission was PHP 75 per person; parking is available nearby, convenient if you arrive by car.Visitor center: Friendly, informative staff at the Visitor Center who helped with maps, tickets, and directions.Shrine of Rizal: The Rizal Shrine is moving and well-presented, with exhibits that clearly tell the story of José Rizal and the wider history of the Philippines.Underground cells: The underground cells and dungeons are a must-visit — stark and sobering, they effectively convey the harsh realities prisoners faced.Time needed: Plan about 1.5 hours to walk the grounds, visit the exhibits, and explore the cells.Atmosphere: The fort has a somber, reflective atmosphere that’s both educational and emotionally impactful.Tips:Wear comfortable shoes; paths and stairs can be uneven.Visit in the morning to avoid midday heat and crowds.Bring water and a camera (photos allowed in most areas).Overall: an essential historical stop in Manila for anyone interested in Philippine history — informative, well-run, and deeply moving.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-31T06:16:44.096947634Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:95:\"This landmark defensive fortress features a museum commemorating the national hero José Rizal.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:5;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJDXUM9QPKlzMRDOajr3iHEoQ\";s:4:\"name\";s:17:\"Manila Ocean Park\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.5793088;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.9724475;s:7:\"address\";s:78:\"666 Behind, Quirino Grandstand, Ermita, Manila, 1000 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.2;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:18266;s:7:\"reviews\";i:18266;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:494:\"places/ChIJDXUM9QPKlzMRDOajr3iHEoQ/photos/AVoNoXRJ3dksHOPDQtjUlwmsrXfD9US859HnrLeBPFznvobZ75xTFJWmNEukiNT2iigiNdVsxmqTT_EvK8Har8Vgsz08NBGxjLRwxsYCgkaRnMvlhwTNBtnLrcA7LfQtxIN08WxbQGtHstQRq0oDPbDj5Rv6D-KDHRogjZ94A2P4TDt1D6W0ZbpVCXUEfqs6XCRNni4kYAvRRz4aMqZxWLHqkOL2f9Nh2B0kH4U1RzkkXkKgbDYSVIKCrBnWOETaYoY-O7S71nn4C6Xfohcb1ud-lgc5l2Hup_tcMqPO-_tuTCNbF0uhKzFoajw6rOs8Z7nKPlygTdxYck_XhiJwLrP0eqJKd6X62O6ac4hQYkMo5p8xBTmGaoMHFqEdNjFsRVxyaG1b12wVNCkHHjQ9kEgDfYbYCGQ3yf-UEMyhQpcU4AZwCTr4u7if1jwkqsyAhFBb\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:494:\"places/ChIJDXUM9QPKlzMRDOajr3iHEoQ/photos/AVoNoXRJ3dksHOPDQtjUlwmsrXfD9US859HnrLeBPFznvobZ75xTFJWmNEukiNT2iigiNdVsxmqTT_EvK8Har8Vgsz08NBGxjLRwxsYCgkaRnMvlhwTNBtnLrcA7LfQtxIN08WxbQGtHstQRq0oDPbDj5Rv6D-KDHRogjZ94A2P4TDt1D6W0ZbpVCXUEfqs6XCRNni4kYAvRRz4aMqZxWLHqkOL2f9Nh2B0kH4U1RzkkXkKgbDYSVIKCrBnWOETaYoY-O7S71nn4C6Xfohcb1ud-lgc5l2Hup_tcMqPO-_tuTCNbF0uhKzFoajw6rOs8Z7nKPlygTdxYck_XhiJwLrP0eqJKd6X62O6ac4hQYkMo5p8xBTmGaoMHFqEdNjFsRVxyaG1b12wVNCkHHjQ9kEgDfYbYCGQ3yf-UEMyhQpcU4AZwCTr4u7if1jwkqsyAhFBb\";i:1;s:473:\"places/ChIJDXUM9QPKlzMRDOajr3iHEoQ/photos/AVoNoXRgY96I2pyoKTuJQqaWVrATl4I9PlYail7yMyWQ-sji_JyW6d9FpLhY90TKVv1UZbppQDPqUsLjxRb4dC4qS9oVKn4iQdorsKiwb4VorrJmPu0JhHl7-4tXYyA33SahC5SNJHCcN7OeSvcECfFxtTkRhpOkh0tIROaW3XrivNm7qBdsyZUlTu4Vxhe8gRJVVsBkjJv-LlB1GLeJaUFTNMezbi4Oengc6XFxuhbu2yJWe8Jg2CVvzflMmr0gNVFy1RHb7IqRif-VPkUW5UlmI1QdufJ6A05ZJl5S_brhApWOYEitQtr4udv6UVKbphi1DV03itoE24nl59E2M0_fAoWN3BpYFCbpuLYjVUWGcj7SQG2fRkYmZjmwJEV-U7t5qavjGzQ0C0RXBmUuNuq9MaQXHUnYq0MVVfH5nXN5OJI\";i:2;s:478:\"places/ChI