AR2ej-4LJ0okdD9cF7xLwOTxmU7adsZKg\";i:5;s:494:\"places/ChIJeWcu0hfKlzMRnYOqfe-gowY/photos/AVoNoXQeyJjs_vve-7jEhFHQw83Eg_xqqCA9utsFcc0B5VKhaqmTjUsdN_O__bKa0rk___F3j7j38LrPjSdXEn0j8V8EZUwmLN5Bpqp3bA1RagL7ItEiFVDTPjYUkO0RxBhOcFY9SY20Q3laHJjaP_hCirxwQnGu6nHlX7cUltugKINR_XZ0PSXvyKX2f4dWvKjB7_SKykGw6WqoWbOWbUAnk78sXbxJn3wv6n6SBBZG0uJ_s-K2AA5uGR0vzdQq6F3xU8GbY-cgRu9w6xJPs_tVEKnFyLDIZ3t9jFDyR1CiN_eHu6hKWe9MPH1PrUAnXYP1r5WAiNlDaRGozmLkTX1zCHV3gwRv1zw5L-IRPxmP4c0aqCrVxOls-tD8in9oLQTe01cXBkD_AvRTUjNpkCW501KEShwNDCMmvl9zL9WMyKXNF5ztcs53QbZ-TvQhnNoa\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:9:\"Ezio Tech\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVjiMOelQstOch5Z0TNE7voTc9llX0kWWbKgoSwERUbffdeHRK1=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:382:\"A beautiful cathedral in the heart of Intramuros, Manila.\n\nIt is easy to find and a good place to visit while exploring the area. Inside is simple but still nice, with beautiful statues and stained glass.\n\nI liked learning about its history, especially knowing a church has stood here since the 16th century.\n\nWorth a quick visit, and it looks beautiful at night with the lights on.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-24T05:15:08.503512669Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"SHINOBI XMIE A7\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXpYYWmAnJbDzhJVpBBIDAvwipUH9Ckm1sUY-3Q3cDgColmhitM=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:434:\"Minor Basilica and Metropolitañ Cathed\nNice\"If you’re visiting Fort Santiago, I highly recommend walking over to the Minor Basilica and Metropolitan Cathedral of the Immaculate Conception. The architecture and interior details are breathtaking! It’s a wonderful place to learn about local history while taking in the beautiful atmosphere. Plus, there are plenty of picturesque spots perfect for photos. Definitely worth a visit!\"\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-08-09T03:15:45.908800485Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:11:\"Carlos Neri\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVgBcUeLifqYRWzq_kTu56umSri7vtVrkTzliiOavX4mr0Wr7GGKQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:1238:\"A Sacred Space Worthy of Our Lady\n\nThe Manila Cathedral is truly a solemn and holy place — a beautiful tribute to the Immaculate Conception of the Blessed Virgin Mary. Stepping inside, you immediately feel the weight of centuries of faith and devotion.\n\nDaily Masses are held every morning, and 12:10 PM Mass. The homilies are consistently enlightening and inspiring, and each weekday Mass ends with a blessing of religious articles — a small but meaningful touch that keeps you coming back. The music elevates the entire experience: the choir is reverent and skilled, accompanied by the largest pipe organ in the Philippines, which fills the entire cathedral with a sound that is nothing short of breathtaking.\n\nThere’s also daily confession at 10pm-12nn every weekday.\n\nOn Sundays, the air conditioning is on, which is a blessing in Manila’s heat! However, it does get very crowded — monobloc seats are available on the sides, but the lines can get long, so come early if you want a good seat inside. The good news is that the audio and visual setup is excellent, with clear sound and live feed screens so you can follow the Mass comfortably wherever you’re seated.\n\nA must-visit for Catholics and history lovers alike. ?\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-23T09:23:28.267457069Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:7:\"JOHANNA\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXrJ9kBh7SlemfYUGHSHPAiSD3hkFsshP_sn5C7KOnGp6Ph5X10=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:301:\"This church is beautiful! As a catholic myself, I can say this is one of the most beautiful church I ever seen in my whole life. The architecture, the vibes, the atmosphere. It really make me connected with my beliefs.\n\nI love how these environments managed well, everything feels so serene and clean.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-07T03:20:06.576339108Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:18:\"Tyrone Jann Flores\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWill_2b2qIe_hSCou4yBs-FkGWhIBFcE5-WqhE9Y9jkh-t6Qo=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:1167:\"Attended a wedding at the Manila Cathedral and it truly remains one of the most beautiful and iconic churches in the country. The architecture, stained-glass windows, and overall atmosphere make it a very solemn and memorable venue for weddings. There\'s something special about celebrating such an important occasion in a church with so much history and character.\n\nOne thing we noticed during our visit was the heat. Since the wedding was held during the hotter months, it became quite humid and uncomfortable while guests were waiting for the ceremony to start. The air conditioning was only turned on shortly before the ceremony and was turned off not long after. We understand that this may have been based on the package or schedule arranged by the couple, but it would have been nice if there was a bit more flexibility, especially for special events like weddings. Many guests were already feeling the effects of the heat before the ceremony even began.\n\nThat said, the beauty, solemnity, and significance of the Manila Cathedral still make it a wonderful place to celebrate a wedding. Despite the weather, it was a memorable and meaningful experience overall.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-05-30T15:19:32.868268778Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:99:\"Built in 1571, this historic church is known for its ornate architecture & visits by several popes.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:10;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJk5OKFRDKlzMRwQwO9gF-vL0\";s:4:\"name\";s:71:\"Minor Basilica and National Shrine of St Lorenzo Ruiz ( Binondo Church)\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.600161499999997;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.97458890000001;s:7:\"address\";s:72:\"1006 Plaza Lorenzo Ruiz, Binondo, Manila, 1006 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.6;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:3581;s:7:\"reviews\";i:3581;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:492:\"places/ChIJk5OKFRDKlzMRwQwO9gF-vL0/photos/AVoNoXTnxBxRtwCr8D0IOmyeW3JlyB1WZ6M3p9iS1M2pDYDw3FVSaIsvMWiYNjowoIIzei66ssEcu7XqVbG9MpRMZ6xrXoY754Jdm_N44bkIs-6WG5GpZcz4AoVP338ORXkNP1dUg-wJXjXMmRyxjuITDIp4OWy9Qh2FosIu6kILCwbz7cw_3YWevt8RM62rkelS3_Uj58JxsxX_8kTIdD_9LFb3CsLVKPqmMkeYH8D3z-BZ4uwhl6A9JfrbmWKDr4hs3M5q5vjJjV1syXz4sLoIao83NPtX7wUd551sD1r0Q2pvb1TN-NHqliCeLZYtqU3SVkPrf7iUlZro9ut-c4014RgqLnXc7KEGQl9jCHsqY58RqjpuwKjPBBoqSOhZ_FhRjbtZlcrTcLtQizq5twHIoj1wZ2lCjBCFKjMSI-fIzy0Tghco8wonM9b5_EdyoQ\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:492:\"places/ChIJk5OKFRDKlzMRwQwO9gF-vL0/photos/AVoNoXTnxBxRtwCr8D0IOmyeW3JlyB1WZ6M3p9iS1M2pDYDw3FVSaIsvMWiYNjowoIIzei66ssEcu7XqVbG9MpRMZ6xrXoY754Jdm_N44bkIs-6WG5GpZcz4AoVP338ORXkNP1dUg-wJXjXMmRyxjuITDIp4OWy9Qh2FosIu6kILCwbz7cw_3YWevt8RM62rkelS3_Uj58JxsxX_8kTIdD_9LFb3CsLVKPqmMkeYH8D3z-BZ4uwhl6A9JfrbmWKDr4hs3M5q5vjJjV1syXz4sLoIao83NPtX7wUd551sD1r0Q2pvb1TN-NHqliCeLZYtqU3SVkPrf7iUlZro9ut-c4014RgqLnXc7KEGQl9jCHsqY58RqjpuwKjPBBoqSOhZ_FhRjbtZlcrTcLtQizq5twHIoj1wZ2lCjBCFKjMSI-fIzy0Tghco8wonM9b5_EdyoQ\";i:1;s:476:\"places/ChIJk5OKFRDKlzMRwQwO9gF-vL0/photos/AVoNoXRuzOvDxAhbXV1kAITNguAZvdC3mkpQiTp4Kd1tU9U5fOHeGCkExrhxreuKWWfHdAkzR_JaH3L1xsmnKOOun3BG9rY-vaYRYG638Ox_ZrNW1kc591RzdsSPIjtrVY8yMPVri3ni-PZ4DLmYuVI1ii2lWZHiBmghpQuDjxrCo0S_5Vf457S3UI6cQzfswaRAumbCUG2jxt314sR4nI2vh3jdxJy2H7rnlGpYz9GJ5STQu1LMK2hyToEQS_rBnuuoGsCul9V658foiY7OVQc-Go374idQhLALeLbQauijb9v0-Z7gn-k4bpj9QZEuQZXP3gxR3ezaY-AbqtXJEjDemyzGLY8NSxA6QpD2lnsS8fTeMG_81tQhmzpxFqkHfjTmrB4pkxhaU17nAQ2q8eciwJTcoRe6_ClRGlrxT6djb9i7RQ\";i:2;s:476:\"places/ChIJk5OKFRDKlzMRwQwO9gF-vL0/photos/AVoNoXSOML8eMy5O5zA