h3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKmLmab2tWgWVOxBbfA20GH1xyrzlysrKzpwIJ98k-olizseYY=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:687:\"I’ve had multiple visits in this church already. Google review only allows one but I’ve been there during weekdays, Weekends, public holidays and different times of the day in each visit. I also visited while mass is ongoing or before or after the mass. Their facebook page is also updated regularly so you can also check it out for the mass schedules and other sacraments you want. Normally we visit during Holy Week (public holidays) and weekends for Sunday mass and on Weekdays for Confession and feast day of San Lorenzo Ruiz or other saints and events/feasts to hear mass on those days. Days we just pass by are when we accompany friends for Visita Iglesia, usually balikbayans.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-07-10T19:40:59.800225616Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"Hobart Ferry\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXrNJm3Z5w8vkyAKcDkZC6IncLEJB6W9373iYDfNgb4Rl0fYeKA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:395:\"I visited Binondo Church and the place felt really peaceful despite being in the busy streets of Binondo. The church is beautiful and has a very historic vibe since it’s one of the oldest churches in Manila. It’s a nice place to stop by, say a quick prayer, and take a moment to relax before exploring the food spots around Binondo. Definitely worth visiting if you’re in the area. ⛪?\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-10T08:49:33.455084631Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"romelyn dueñas\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjX8-OUWlHsfA6-wR1_3tLTdih4kgrDW5sk0usCYXXistmI6_M4Gng=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:285:\"Amidst the crowd outside, you\'ll find peace and comfort here. The old church is well-maintained and patrons are very kind. Just please wear decent clothes. It\'s just sad to see people not minding their clothing and food when entering here. It\'s not a tourist attraction, it\'s a church.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-29T03:09:18.119758253Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:16:\"Karl Gerald Saul\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWLCFPNxp2Nbya_xFoXy8gOtffEYzFi17cTlmAd8H6U-p7ZxsoG=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:843:\"In Nine Frames: Binondo Church\n\nThe Minor Basilica & National Shrine of Saint Lawrence Ruiz of Manila.\n\nIn the heart of Binondo stands a church that has witnessed centuries of devotion, war, rebuilding, and unwavering faith. Founded in 1596 by Dominican priests, this sanctuary became a spiritual home for the Chinese-Filipino community and later honored the first Filipino saint, Saint Lorenzo Ruiz.\n\nThrough earthquakes, fires, and World War II, it rose again and again — its stone walls holding stories of prayers whispered in different languages, candles lit in hope, and faith that refuses to fade.\n\nIn nine frames, I captured not just architecture — but history carved in stone and faith that stands the test of time.\n\nNikon Z30 + NIKKOR Z DX 18-140mm VR\n\n#BinondoChurch\n#FaithInFrames\n#KAGESAVisuals\n#ChurchPhotography\n#InNineFrames\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-20T17:15:50.470191909Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:3:\"Bek\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUOKMwVoSpafxW10MDXlxq7zXVj0ixGN39XbdrcZz4x3Eh0GWE=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:174:\"A solemn place to pray in the midst of the busyness of Binondo. Staff is also very nice to turn on the electric fan for us even if we arrived few minutes before closing time.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-11T20:20:27.197361615Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:98:\"Landmark granite church with a 16th-century bell tower, featuring regular masses & self-led tours.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:11;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJ4_WFMX7JlzMRJOkBCvft38A\";s:4:\"name\";s:36:\"Manila Zoological & Botanical Garden\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.5648118;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.98836960000001;s:7:\"address\";s:60:\"Adriatico St, Malate, Manila, 1004 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:3.7;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:6253;s:7:\"reviews\";i:6253;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:478:\"places/ChIJ4_WFMX7JlzMRJOkBCvft38A/photos/AVoNoXRWMlTbB6Ds4JIfMeyXH7elvB_vdhh2xQuVPGGS3L08JG13fPyh_wVvGD4_K_fuaNhSM3_9SeUml2sD8YRcpXX7FnQ03ib3rPEhnZMsIIL-XyRwww04TrvU3lqTser0g4kLc-h-vNCuiRJrWljqN8PIpArJMPgtVd9FVovxgFeTy-GrJFnRcEd87EBUE7SVDV61hbN0OWE4W0gun24bZeXbacLepxBNoiOczhRUL0SpdVoQSUTx_pTwPLnHsJgv8GPKls1Et90f8jhgq0UhxZGF5W4cVOo-T2Y3Lsl6SI5MzZ7f9Jc0OABzhn68LZKpKWDg6EZKfL9dZg7UilEOxkMHQpymW9VHgsgEoo3pr4nwgBCLDqassY2hmm91-SxPQJ7ia8IvzqJB190446zS8zFB94McE5GY6mWCRuSbd_zKO0Dn\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:478:\"places/ChIJ4_WFMX7JlzMRJOkBCvft38A/photos/AVoNoXRWMlTbB6Ds4JIfMeyXH7elvB_vdhh2xQuVPGGS3L08JG13fPyh_wVvGD4_K_fuaNhSM3_9SeUml2sD8YRcpXX7FnQ03ib3rPEhnZMsIIL-XyRwww04TrvU3lqTser0g4kLc-h-vNCuiRJrWljqN8PIpArJMPgtVd9FVovxgFeTy-GrJFnRcEd87EBUE7SVDV61hbN0OWE4W0gun24bZeXbacLepxBNoiOczhRUL0SpdVoQSUTx_pTwPLnHsJgv8GPKls1Et90f8jhgq0UhxZGF5W4cVOo-T2Y3Lsl6SI5MzZ7f9Jc0OABzhn68LZKpKWDg6EZKfL9dZg7UilEOxkMHQpymW9VHgsgEoo3pr4nwgBCLDqassY2hmm91-SxPQJ7ia8IvzqJB190446zS8zFB94McE5GY6mWCRuSbd_zKO0Dn\";i:1;s:478:\"places/ChIJ4_WFMX7JlzMRJOkBCvft38A/photos/AVoNoXS7QCftxaqAN8cwQOfQGDJCkmjfQd7VSLcTQrNCIKPq8LP2c_8faQMACVQ7moMDk1MCbYTDAdjCbaJLukksln8hQj2Rwd8Wt6B5DEYJ2RcVBAGvF4_Rvw1ch_wVVbBLkj75QzZxLhbpmmcO94OOjh9QfUeBg2Xgw6ZBcHzTAOOvwxsOXGHCiGaLoRCZAuxeqDWzNJ3U59xr3m8_NlQbK8PkU1HrrSUq88kce9l6rOno1LO4NjgLNcLzj14ZakHSDVlvoBa15YOaLI-f6kSPBowBJNxCiWvs-Eho4tj4iLbSY6DcWWb1UXOhOx9-B9ZhsqDGxWxnNiSK-ssOsX0OHTX31Nz0KGutwIyTpEq3m6yQAR5RrnA0_vEljqUdojLK1zMQKY6l21