ent of the Philippines. Guides went into incredible detail and aside from a few phrases was entirely in English. And it’s all free! Took about 2.5 hours from start to finish, but well worth it. Facilities include restrooms and a museum shop at the end. Recommend!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-08T14:02:47.279360858Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"Frank Solorzano\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXRzT_sP2qgg9oxqm7fU16ZGENW5GStwYJr3qGOXGMUMd3g2IzD=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:238:\"Very impressive museum.  I didn\'t read the description correctly for the tour. I thought I\'d visit the actual Malacañang Palace, but rather it was a couple of historical residences.  It was still very informative and well worth the trip.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-11T19:24:55.141860420Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:7:\"Fon BKK\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXr8xj8tOHYwVh1sTnncOTiQ3dfF6jjw4JqmxtCUAM53ZrVaJvy=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:222:\"Most excellent guides - was here as only one on the malacang heritage tour - free / nice on hot day. Anyone can book online up to a three business days in advance. Lovely museums. They still take tour even with one person.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2024-08-11T10:48:45.476055Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:24:\"ShonCecileShaira Herrera\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXoU56XE3RivLUWHGGHgpR-A9yxJ2r-fXeQ9TSbPkSxTYjnLUz8=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:265:\"This place is awesome. This is the presidential house of our president, the place is very special and unique and its look very large palace with garden outside. If you experience to go inside you feel very special and its privileges\' to see the structure and setup.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-01-28T15:54:17.420048882Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Rhodora Manga\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWCT1iKLJT_qz4qcOKGjTCFm9evmjRyMGN9q8NhiQfYuNbvDw50Ow=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:488:\"I brought my Polish date here. And oh boy, it did not disappoint. He had fun. We were only 5 in a group and the tour guide is very knowledgeable of the historical background of the items in display in the museum. IF YOU HAVE FOREIGN VISITORS, BRING THEM HERE. You just have to email the palace museum and tours coordinator your desired day and time to visit. Entrance is for free. Foreign nationals must affix a scanned copy of the face of their passport with the request to visit. Enjoy!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:27:\"2020-02-08T07:58:18.890950Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:92:\"Presidential museum & library showcasing Philippine politics, culture & history, with tours.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:16;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJdQPKJQXKlzMRR6XZGbXDUhU\";s:4:\"name\";s:9:\"Chinatown\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.601030100000001;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.9785194;s:7:\"address\";s:65:\"913 Ongpin St, Santa Cruz, Manila, 1003 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.1;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:577;s:7:\"reviews\";i:577;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:494:\"places/ChIJdQPKJQXKlzMRR6XZGbXDUhU/photos/AVoNoXSKRqBG9ttif39n6dOWvdD9ZbKV_HWPCREIjTGMoaITHvJiLj8WBaCGbU8qrgWpExYUs4FvSsRiFwZhK7S7qft_bhfg-BTzdyLKz1Plac3TyiOkqpFsPuyDA-7lhR1dmxBAIszQWSZYJ2EcUQmG_nV-0GaMth3R3rR34LAhPKLtQANgqt0RYuPtvl_rBCoJR6LcTKhRmZ6Xcnnb_9yzO7u4PckLgxxRtuI1vyBsuleLhWr2yqyeP3uCEDxEQdIS93KPBB5vfdzLzczbn8kzvdtK851pqMmryvUvgMW-UhCS5_2yEWwMQfiPhDOFabAuJiAgeJ7Y_0HvQj2xSBQGKmUahn5WilTWUA1ILNO8emeGrJZDY9UPNmZ8Ei4lDQ4guAj2DAZnzyXNvpgtu5s2IC0QqbwbgkVmR5lGeC_HI_e--jY9CcsEedyY35ri1TQ1\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:49