BXKmPyvaz4mLT4flJBiq5U_RFGAhnn1aSRBctjYbSInvQxwB29IsAsLN0o88eiUPM1u_XWbVYhK50KM9RnVH7oaLs-xyLDgz3-YDDv1SupppriDxICwG7KepPgm-8fu547Wt0Liowa2s401ve2vwFeAtkOx4C3zeRxwT1AqfwQgP_g2Zl6QPCmMXvFscx1Af4snVBEIzhJ_vc8bb7LoXEAxKqar7j9_esGb_6DZZ94qOqFqPgx26cXU9k2FZoUTfGvebpAgr6nds8dZ8J__GzyA0BD-In11BiOmNhXbzJW5vJsRqjQPbIu5wjKLscBMq1x_fX2AzkvxraW9Ho5ATxZT0XeqjFsWxBgqN_dN2\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Irene Basubas\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV2-OLugtISo_71HHSwMPu20Spxx8-taKC3Dy9FV7jmTlJM2u2K=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba2\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:292:\"Better place to spend time for refreshing and rewind. I find this place for relaxation when when life\'s feels overwhelmed. I\'d love the sound of the sea and the shirping sound of birds. I don\'t care about the sound of people\'s gossips around me. I only care how I can relax hahah.☺️☺️\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-09T21:41:57.987047475Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:8:\"Niki Poh\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWy4C0SIEwukNVb01R7W2Uxg04Pk3tGhOcgV0MAbLIDw-Pfrm8=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:401:\"1 of the best sunsets in Metro Manila, with vibrant orange and pink skies over the water.\nIt’s beautiful and easy to access, especially along Baywalk, but can get crowded and a bit messy at times.\n** Dont allow to bring drink or food in..\nAs you exit Manila Bay after sunset, you’re often greeted by local vendors selling snacks, drinks, and souvenirs. It adds a lively, street-market feel... ?\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-21T05:27:32.766079315Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:13:\"Dineth Perera\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:123:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXY_-XcrQRiiCou6Q8ymfPwXjUpCEEhEjbd4p7OA6vzOFFPJxUr=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:462:\"If you want to see the famous Manila Bay sunset, this is the best place to do it. The white dolomite sand makes the whole area look very clean and bright compared to how it used to be. It\'s a great spot for a late afternoon stroll or for taking photos. Entrance is free, and the area is well-maintained by the staff. Just a heads-up: no swimming is allowed, and they are quite strict about the cleaning. Definitely worth a visit for the views and the sea breeze!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-08T11:28:48.999036586Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:15:\"Jerry Gutierrez\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLYIMckypFWGe4WIAHD7SlC8zfEICJtBpos0pKKZRU-H3MNwA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:994:\"Absolutely stunning. It’s the kind of sunset that makes you stop and put your phone down for a second—though you’ll definitely want to take a few photos. I was honestly impressed by the maintenance. There is a strict no-plastic and no-glass policy, and they are thorough with inspections at the entrance. Though I wouldn\'t jump in the Bay for health reasons.\n\nI’ll be honest, finding your way in can be a little confusing at first. Don\'t be afraid to ask the security personnel for guidance; they’ll steer you in the right direction.\nThe public restrooms (CR) weren’t operational during my visit. Pro-tip: There is a Starbucks right across the street. It’s a reliable spot to grab a coffee and use the facilities if nature calls.\n\nYou’ll notice a few vendors and massage therapists near the entrance. They may occasionally ask for a bit of spare change. A polite \"no thank you\" is usually all it takes if you aren\'t interested.\n\nI rented a moped for quick parking and departure.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-03T11:01:35.877922401Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:5:\"Trina\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVKP6Xe89dvn_GlRYrkKeZzdBwBkNNPFwMw_VtLZsvLgOihTWWBJQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:629:\"Went here for sunset and it’s actually not bad. I didn’t expect much, but the view surprised me. The sunset over Manila Bay still hits differently — the sky slowly changing colors while the breeze from the sea makes the moment feel a little more peaceful in the middle of the busy city.\n\nIt’s probably one of the easiest places in Metro Manila if you just want to see the beach and catch a sunset without going too far. Sometimes you don’t need to travel hours to enjoy a nice view.\n\nGoogle rating: around 4.2⭐️ — and honestly, it’s not a bad spot at all if you’re just looking for a quick sunset escape. ?\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-03-16T12:39:38.862098847Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:94:\"Bordered by open-air cafes, this long, bayside walkway is a popular place to watch the sunset.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}i:19;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJG6WEGPjJlzMRQouYY2zJvYQ\";s:4:\"name\";s:94:\"Minor Basilica of San Sebastian and Shrine of Our Lady of Mount Carmel (Archdiocese of Manila)\";s:3:\"lat\";d:14.5997001;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.9890595;s:7:\"address\";s:68:\"Pasaje del Carmen St, Quiapo, Manila, 1001 Metro Manila, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.7;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:1484;s:7:\"reviews\";i:1484;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:478:\"places/ChIJG6WEGPjJlzMRQouYY2zJvYQ/photos/AVoNoXSU6-A5Nb7iuuJC7N2hjc7GgSBhKKh1O45GnpFR9YZf1R2us8xGESP_KnYnPXi6IlkdbiQFvxVm_d3LWTG9z8KOkqQgdIECznpGvAvTnwQlGICo_V4EUfvHI_qVBADzMiBdgTx5GCvrs3JAKtDA4NOpieJPQ-xobSsPuntKSHr-8PeApOfoGjprtLoxthpXz34d9vmThbKOuWyknySztNdwruq20d9kjLZFfUljVKkUj_h1QJ6HX8Sx3SO4K0BR60xC8XE4eVHTxqUsFwumlaqWgSDzNHIZHsudiwQzR87pz3EqD38JYLIaVwkrndeNAJgQKL9Nk_gVOJHllAA313Ha6PLydDoel1Ua81B4hNgxTlZ0jP5z6aXvFFYPtoFHAL1uPCQoHFxGteu0Z-zQMnPJyY2-asgFw_1aF87LkY-WX3_-\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:6:{i:0;s:478:\"places/ChIJG6WEGPjJlzMRQouYY2zJvYQ/photos/AVoNo