oNoXR169BV2nPkzNXW47DAgj8MqqPvUwM7LSJ3-KsxzYNXQElopSc1JBlnf6j3kukdOnwGxvkT71ibCZpjO04D8GSON_4ncxvyFWceG53Q85uBbK3XmBvkIXqXCjy1pJlOc3Tw9eFO09gukBilXUFetU1pz2z67YLGCod3BLgTCkwqjV3xCkw7EH78flWVCMjMW90LWwsVPDpqfpMxPTk1F-lIyAN3bmhVAkaUAOBeuEvypvn6KSCviqnT9Hw3pU-I2C5CsMi6IFIgfLBB3AP7t7FVFYkuc9nCn8E8WajMOvjfs6OhSQj6LWck4VBwfV_05CIJJIGRQKZWPp6T-cZdT33FDcci4ZJg8skYnnZ-DedxW0e2fi9td-kz2QwqXydFq4eA4tvwnxXLHbtKjRxwgnWqV5-93nebaL6XpsNwGGdYjA\";i:5;s:473:\"places/ChIJG6WEGPjJlzMRQouYY2zJvYQ/photos/AVoNoXTD1_3cf3MZ7II5WhEiXCc5pO12M9ledSgH9IFAXY1oY7pa7PZe_cEol6IqHM4ud9CCuLUw7BUGce1681i6tp65Q0LGnrI8HHhR8LJ1Jlu7FAz2EC6TNuM2_oQCdLVBT-x4K3IrEphflb-CPTXVVbQm793gP0Jz2zvgm9SGN1vrjpVUWlGXQwOvgLGbvChBTcCZM7yIOogFSEWky0-1xmEnXAYNkWmNj8fRgPwW6DwI79o7JECG-NHJerXEcMcUfUVyMKmmDnsDTAoKaHXnGCZUOpMaEJyJB6SgBFL5RuygF9iOm8goHPQ53kRkkt96F0AtgE3_SnSyG8SbPlvmxa4_mBbiBHP5NiveOTvRhpabhGMXfn7e6mCRMGcD1G7oqk_yIvKfgV_ix5mySk50LMBliWiRIFPsRNHTI2NlzUs\";}s:12:\"reviews_data\";a:5:{i:0;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:8:\"Manny Yu\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXg-da5a8zn8eyarfcNq2GYSnijPq0sUNl8cm346u4c6jhtgcg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba8\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:1280:\"Bisita Iglesia 2026 Number Five: San Sebastian Basilica.\n\nBisita Iglesia 2026. Historic churches in Metro Manila Part 2.\n\nIt has long been reputed that Gustave Eiffel, the French engineer behind the Eiffel Tower and the steel structure within the Statue of Liberty, was involved in the design and construction of San Sebastián, but this was never confirmed.\n\nThe prefabricated steel sections that would compose the church were manufactured in Binche, Belgium. According to historian Ambeth Ocampo, the knockdown steel parts were ordered from the Societe anonyme des Enterprises de Travaux Publiques in Brussels. In all, 52 metric tons (51 long tons; 57 short tons) of prefabricated steel sections were transported in eight separate shipments from Belgium to the Philippines, the first shipment arriving in 1888. Belgian engineers supervised the assembly of the church, the first column of which was erected on September 11, 1890. The walls were filled with mixed sand, gravel, and cement. The stained glass windows were imported from the Heinrich Oidtmann Company, a German stained glass firm, while local artisans assisted in applying the finishing touches.\n\nOur most beautiful church with the dramatic moody shadows and soaring arched ceiling during this year\'s Bisita Iglesia.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-03T22:06:36.147375665Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:1;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:17:\"Yours truly, Tony\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVz-jGr4Nbq5niehM8It3HT8msPkqdLPDevfqtVdo3FPe0O2ng=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:193:\"Very astonishing church. The façade is almost made of iron and metal sheets. You will feel the solemnity once inside the church. And for those who want a peace of mind, please visit the place.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-20T13:20:20.636240850Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:2;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:12:\"Altus Vision\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:122:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVFl43EklYmRqgaWPOS9Poxovb6stDKqVxDZlUOkzpaiowCw4w=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:380:\"The design of the church is super unique. You can already see the belfry from far distance and the gothic design of the church gave me an exhilarating feeling. The interior is also a masterpiece, the ceiling, tho old and a little corroded, the artwork can still be recognised and the erosions only add to its beautiful history.\n\nOne of the best Church to visit in the Philippines!\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-02-21T05:38:07.183490057Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:3;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"iain smith\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:120:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJCN_vYlffanLBt2DbAE0eF1E5y3TTKQPOXob3N4WBGec3LPA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba7\";s:6:\"rating\";i:4;s:4:\"text\";s:218:\"Large basilica with 2 big towers in front\nUnfortunately it was under renovations outside with lots of scaffolding\nBut inside wow really beautiful gothic style artitecture  but just missed mass so not many people inside\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-06-03T02:03:51.977557313Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}i:4;a:6:{s:6:\"author\";s:10:\"Liza Viray\";s:6:\"avatar\";s:125:\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUmjFpob1Ukl58QbsfBGCfkuJj6a2eJ9lK6YRO9mAstZS20hBvfQw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5\";s:6:\"rating\";i:5;s:4:\"text\";s:134:\"Needs immediate paint job on the whole outdoor but still a very nice church. Medieval vibes because of its Gothic Architecture design.\";s:9:\"timestamp\";s:30:\"2026-04-02T06:14:37.885839091Z\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"Google\";}}s:17:\"editorial_summary\";s:96:\"Built in 1891, this striking Gothic church has steel vaulting, stained-glass windows & 2 towers.\";s:6:\"source\";s:6:\"google\";}}',1787978667),('laravel-cache-rapidapi_tourist_attraction_15.641_120.428','a:20:{i:0;a:15:{s:2:\"id\";s:27:\"ChIJyfWtgr-1ljMR1hWQhPpR_40\";s:4:\"name\";s:27:\"Santa Ignacia People\'s Park\";s:3:\"lat\";d:15.6142053;s:3:\"lng\";d:120.43394479999999;s:7:\"address\";s:50:\"Poblacion West, Santa Ignacia, Tarlac, Philippines\";s:8:\"category\";s:12:\"google_place\";s:4:\"type\";s:8:\"landmark\";s:6:\"rating\";d:4.1;s:18:\"user_ratings_total\";i:11;s:7:\"reviews\";i:11;s:15:\"photo_reference\";s:478:\"places/ChIJyfWtgr-1ljMR1hWQhPpR_40/photos/AVoNoXRnB0Av-y8vcSxjsvaUmDBf5meJorft1mk0LeXevhS-QwzR4D-txsViG7CEBKDK8zlEGMpHKyG1Cn1SW7l7uYYoff0FfyxuHksxSBG5d3zIdp-DJWv48nC-9z2_6bcBUz3aJS2Jub7wUOoazf7ZJr6s334kXhnWWE24SlHrWKd3mlYWkubfcvbCfytUqnjLpxfkBDorIPgicjSnaUnosFYJ98GdjAKq-DKx01yk0oiJ5M7stIS82EEQELoXvS0eld8wQhTz0-YeFUJg6JHTf-ifI8MyaX7HhChhgrwNK9YgAkIg5mun-0FdeaBWv3GyWTTGy1EF0yWnA2yQWaxOrSdcX-yZru9E77YXlJ5lwDmZfXP6Y2HRDmboMKSqg9wRoIR8D_dBx-mUloo8DkHdyeiZHUyQNLkgdV28WO0Vbk6jJUYb\";s:16:\"photo_references\";a:5:{i:0;s:478:\"places/ChIJyfW